===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|lustre}}, from {{der|en|la|lustrum}}, from {{der|en|itc-ola|*loustrom}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. More at {{m|la|lustrum}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{alternative form of|en|lustrum}}: A [[five]]-[[year]] [[period]], [[especially]] {{lb|en|historical}} in [[Roman]] [[context]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1387|translator=John de Trevisa|author=Ranulph Higden|title=Polychronicon|volume=VIII|page=29
|passage=...[[thirty|thritty]] [[year|yere]] of [[VI|vj]]. '''lustres'''...}}
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd|part=II|section=4|member=2|subsection=ii|passage=Mesue and some other Arabians began to reject and reprehend it; upon whose authority, for many following '''lusters''', it was much debased and quite out of request&nbsp;[…].}}

