===Etymology 3===
From {{suf|en|lust|er|id2=agent noun}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|lusts}}{{lb|en|now|_|rare}} One who [[lust]]s, one [[inflamed]] with [[lust]].
#* '''1591''', John Lyly, ''Endimion'', sig. E4v:
#*: ''Eumenides'' But did [[never|neuer]] any [[lovers|Louers]] come [[hither|hether]]?<br>''Geron'' '''Lusters''', but not [[lovers|Louers]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1847|author=Charlotte Brontë|title=Jane Eyre|volume=III|page=124
|passage=...a '''luster''' after power...}}
